---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';
---
<Base title="Write for us: guest posts on AI tools at work" description="Guest post guidelines for practitioners and founders. Publish on how teams in finance, marketing, sales, support, engineering and operations actually use AI tools.">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Write for us</h1>
    <p class="lead">We publish guest posts from practitioners and founders who have actually used the tools they write about, in any part of a business. Free if the article teaches something. Paid placement is available on the <a href="/submit-tool/">advertising page</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose fade-in">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Topics we want</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Honest tool reviews and head to head comparisons (with screenshots)</li>
      <li>How you changed a workflow with AI and what it cost or saved, with numbers</li>
      <li>AI inside a specific function: finance, marketing, sales, support, engineering, HR, legal or operations</li>
      <li>Workflows, prompts and templates a team can copy today</li>
      <li>Lessons from implementing or ripping out a tool</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>1,000 words minimum, original, not published elsewhere</li>
      <li>Written by a named person with a real bio and LinkedIn profile</li>
      <li>One link to your company in the author bio. Contextual links to your product inside the article are a <a href="/submit-tool/">sponsored placement</a>.</li>
      <li>Links to sources, documentation and tools you reference are welcome and stay free</li>
      <li>We edit for clarity and may cut promotional language</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to pitch</h2>
    <p>Send two or three headline ideas plus one sentence on why you are the right person to write each. Use the form below. We reply to every pitch within three business days.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section fade-in">
    <ContactForm kind="guest-pitch" placeholder="Two or three headline ideas, and one line on why you are the right person to write each." />
  </section>
</Base>
